@startuml
autonumber
actor "Client / UI" as Client

participant "Kong Gateway" as Kong
participant "HTTP ClusterIP Service" as HTTPService
participant "Flask App (predict_v5.py)" as FlaskApp
participant "DISDataRAGSystem" as RAGSystem
participant "SentenceTransformer" as Embedder
participant "T5 Generator" as Generator
participant "FAISS Vector Store" as VectorStore
participant "LinearRegression" as MLModel
participant "Data Acquisition Service" as DataAcq
participant "Data Ingestion Service" as DataIng

== Health Check Flow (Public) ==
Client -> Kong : GET /api/prediction/health
activate Kong
Kong -> HTTPService : Route to ClusterIP port 5001
activate HTTPService
HTTPService -> FlaskApp : health()
activate FlaskApp
FlaskApp --> HTTPService : {"status": "healthy", "service": "cap-pdu-prediction"}
deactivate FlaskApp
HTTPService --> Kong : HTTP 200 OK
deactivate HTTPService
Kong --> Client : Health status response
deactivate Kong

== RAG Chat Query Flow (Protected) ==
Client -> Kong : POST /api/prediction/chat\nAuthorization: Bearer {jwt_token}\n{"query": "Total PDU for today"}
activate Kong
Kong -> Kong : Validate Firebase JWT token
activate Kong
note right: Custom jwt-firebase plugin\nvalidates token with Firebase
Kong --> Kong : Extract user claims
deactivate Kong

Kong -> HTTPService : Forward authenticated request\nwith user headers
activate HTTPService
HTTPService -> FlaskApp : chat()
activate FlaskApp

FlaskApp -> FlaskApp : Extract JWT token from headers
FlaskApp -> RAGSystem : set_jwt_token(jwt_token)
activate RAGSystem
RAGSystem --> FlaskApp : Token updated
deactivate RAGSystem

FlaskApp -> RAGSystem : query("Total PDU for today")
activate RAGSystem

RAGSystem -> DataAcq : GET /api/acquisition/realtime\nAuthorization: Bearer {jwt_token}
activate DataAcq
DataAcq --> RAGSystem : Real-time metrics JSON
deactivate DataAcq

RAGSystem -> DataAcq : GET /api/acquisition/aggregate?today=true\nAuthorization: Bearer {jwt_token}
activate DataAcq
DataAcq --> RAGSystem : Aggregated data JSON
deactivate DataAcq

RAGSystem -> RAGSystem : _refresh_data_cache()
activate RAGSystem
note right: Cache data for 2 seconds\nfor performance optimization
RAGSystem --> RAGSystem : Data cached
deactivate RAGSystem

RAGSystem -> Embedder : encode("Total PDU for today")
activate Embedder
Embedder --> RAGSystem : Query embedding vector
deactivate Embedder

RAGSystem -> VectorStore : search(query_embedding, k=5)
activate VectorStore
VectorStore --> RAGSystem : Top 5 similar contexts
deactivate VectorStore

RAGSystem -> RAGSystem : _retrieve_context(query)
activate RAGSystem
note right: Extract relevant context\nfrom cached data and vector search
RAGSystem --> RAGSystem : Contextual information
deactivate RAGSystem

RAGSystem -> Generator : generate(context + query)
activate Generator
Generator --> RAGSystem : Generated response text
deactivate Generator

RAGSystem --> FlaskApp : {"answer": "response", "context": "...", "data_sources": [...]}
deactivate RAGSystem

FlaskApp --> HTTPService : 200 OK with RAG response JSON
deactivate FlaskApp
HTTPService --> Kong : Response with intelligent answer
deactivate HTTPService
Kong --> Client : RAG-powered response
deactivate Kong

== ML Prediction Flow (Protected) ==
Client -> Kong : POST /api/prediction\nAuthorization: Bearer {jwt_token}\n{"timeUnit": "hour", "buckets": [...]}
activate Kong
Kong -> Kong : Validate Firebase JWT token
Kong -> HTTPService : Forward authenticated request
activate HTTPService
HTTPService -> FlaskApp : predict()
activate FlaskApp

FlaskApp -> FlaskApp : predict_pdu_data(request_data)
activate FlaskApp

FlaskApp -> FlaskApp : Extract and validate buckets data
activate FlaskApp
note right: Process 10+ PDU types:\nEntityState, Fire, Collision, Detonation,\nData, ActionRequest, StartResume,\nSetData, Designator, ElectromagneticEmissions
FlaskApp --> FlaskApp : Historical data arrays
deactivate FlaskApp

FlaskApp -> MLModel : fit(X_historical, y_historical)
activate MLModel
MLModel --> FlaskApp : Model trained
deactivate MLModel

FlaskApp -> MLModel : predict(future_x_indices)
activate MLModel
MLModel --> FlaskApp : Predicted values array
deactivate MLModel

FlaskApp -> FlaskApp : Format prediction results
FlaskApp --> FlaskApp : {"predicted_labels": [...], "predicted_values": [...]}
deactivate FlaskApp

FlaskApp --> HTTPService : 200 OK with prediction JSON
deactivate FlaskApp
HTTPService --> Kong : Response with ML predictions
deactivate HTTPService
Kong --> Client : ML prediction response
deactivate Kong

== Chat Status Flow (Public) ==
Client -> Kong : GET /api/prediction/chat/status
activate Kong
Kong -> HTTPService : Route to ClusterIP port 5001
activate HTTPService
HTTPService -> FlaskApp : chat_status()
activate FlaskApp

FlaskApp -> RAGSystem : get_system_status()
activate RAGSystem
RAGSystem -> RAGSystem : Check model readiness
RAGSystem -> RAGSystem : Check data cache status
RAGSystem -> RAGSystem : Check service connectivity
RAGSystem --> FlaskApp : System status dict
deactivate RAGSystem

FlaskApp --> HTTPService : 200 OK with system status
deactivate FlaskApp
HTTPService --> Kong : Response with status info
deactivate HTTPService
Kong --> Client : System status response
deactivate Kong

== Error Handling: Service Unavailable ==
Client -> Kong : POST /api/prediction/chat\nAuthorization: Bearer {jwt_token}
activate Kong
Kong -> HTTPService : Forward authenticated request
activate HTTPService
HTTPService -> FlaskApp : chat()
activate FlaskApp

FlaskApp -> RAGSystem : query("System status")
activate RAGSystem

RAGSystem -> DataAcq : GET /api/acquisition/realtime
activate DataAcq
DataAcq --> RAGSystem : Connection timeout/error
deactivate DataAcq

RAGSystem -> RAGSystem : Handle service unavailable
activate RAGSystem
note right: Graceful degradation:\nUse cached data or\ngenerate fallback response
RAGSystem --> RAGSystem : Fallback context
deactivate RAGSystem

RAGSystem -> Generator : generate(fallback_context + query)
activate Generator
Generator --> RAGSystem : Generated fallback response
deactivate Generator

RAGSystem --> FlaskApp : {"answer": "fallback response", "context": "cached", ...}
deactivate RAGSystem

FlaskApp --> HTTPService : 200 OK with fallback response
deactivate FlaskApp
HTTPService --> Kong : Response with graceful degradation
deactivate HTTPService
Kong --> Client : Intelligent fallback response
deactivate Kong

@enduml